        },
        {
            "name": "charge",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "The scheduled call. One period passes.\nDeliberately the whole of it. No boxes, no payments, no iteration, and so no way to fail once authorization passes \u2014 which matters more than it sounds: a target that rejects gets skipped by the keeper for the rest of its run, and a target that keeps rejecting stops being serviced at all, quietly. Billing that silently stops is worse than billing that is late.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "subscribe",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "pay",
                    "name": "deposit"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Open or top up a subscription, paying this contract.\nA new subscriber starts paid through the current period, so they are billed for periods that begin after they arrive rather than for the one already in progress.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "settle",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "address",
                    "name": "subscriber"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Bill one subscriber for the periods that have passed.\nCallable by anyone, because the caller supplies the box reference and the arithmetic is the same whoever asks. In practice the provider runs it, and it is the counterpart to `charge`: the schedule decides *when* money is owed, this decides *how much* and by whom.\nA subscriber who cannot cover every period owed pays what they have and lapses, rather than blocking. Lapsing is a state, not an error.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "withdraw",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Close a subscription and take back what has not been billed.\nSettlement first: leaving without paying for periods already elapsed would let a subscriber outrun the schedule.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "claim",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "The provider collects what settlement has credited.\nThe provider sends this, so the provider is an available resource by construction. That is the whole reason the money waits here instead of being pushed from the scheduled call.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        }
    ],
